      "why": "Full pipelining gives 1 result/cycle, so at any Fmax it trivially clears the 32 Msps throughput bound and the 0.44 us batch window (32 cycles of latency must fit in 0.44 us, i.e. Fmax >= ~73 MHz, which is comfortable for a CORDIC). This is the family most likely to satisfy all system constraints, so I spend the majority of the budget here. I keep the full n_iter/data_width ranges because accuracy_bits (a maximised objective) and max_abs_err (a hard constraint) are driven by n_iter and data_width, and the LUT/FF area objective is driven by data_width and n_iter — the whole trade-off curve lives in this 2D slice. angle_guard and frac_guard are swept across their full ranges because they trade a few LUTs/FFs against accuracy_bits and are cheap to explore."
    },
    {
      "budget_share": 0.45,
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "choices": [
